# Monstera

A big monstera next to the living room window, with leaves that split more every year.

- Bright, indirect light. Direct sun scorched one leaf last summer.
- Water every one to two weeks.
- It needed a moss pole once it started leaning.
- Wipe the leaves with a damp cloth every month so they can photosynthesize.

It will need a bigger pot by spring. See [Houseplants].

# Home network

The apartment's Wi-Fi had a dead zone in the bedroom, and the router was the one the internet provider sent.

What I did:

- Replaced the provider's router with a mesh system: one unit in the living room, one in the hallway.
- Put the provider's modem in bridge mode so there's only one router.
- Named the network something boring and used a long passphrase.
- Moved the smart plugs to a separate guest network.

Speeds went from about 40 Mbps in the bedroom to about 300 Mbps.

The passphrase is on a card in the drawer by the door, not in this wiki. The [Apartment] page has the rest of the upkeep notes.

# Houseplants

