General care: water when the top inch of soil is dry, and less in winter. Rotate the pots every few weeks so they grow evenly.

Before trips, see the [Packing list]. The outdoor plants are in the [Balcony garden].

# Pothos

The hardest plant to kill. It trails from the top of the bathroom cabinet and loves the humidity.

- Water every week or two, when the leaves start to droop slightly.
- Cuttings root in a glass of water within a few weeks, which makes them easy [Gift ideas].

