# Running

Running three or four days a week, mostly easy pace.

Principles:

- Most runs should be easy enough to hold a conversation.
- Increase weekly mileage by no more than about 10 percent.
- New shoes every 300 to 500 miles.

Current goal: the [Half marathon]. [Priya] and I run together on Saturdays.

After every run, do the [Stretching routine].

# Sleep

The habit with the biggest effect on everything else, including [Running] and mood.

What helps:

- The same wake-up time every day, including weekends
- No screens in the last half hour before bed
- A cool, dark bedroom
- No caffeine after noon

On trips, I use the earplugs and eye mask from the [Packing list] and try to get morning light to adjust to the time zone.

# Stretching routine

Ten minutes after every run, from a physical therapist after a sore knee last year.

1. Standing calf stretch, 30 seconds per side
2. Standing quad stretch, 30 seconds per side
3. Hamstring stretch, lying down with a strap, 30 seconds per side
4. Hip flexor lunge stretch, 30 seconds per side
5. Figure-four glute stretch, 30 seconds per side
6. Foam roll the outside of the thighs, one minute per side

Skipping this is the fastest way to get hurt during [Half marathon] training.

