# Half marathon

Spring half marathon, 13.1 miles. The goal is to finish under two hours without walking.

The [Half marathon training plan] runs twelve weeks. It builds the long run by a mile a week, with a lighter week every fourth week.

Things that matter more than I expected:

- [Sleep] the two nights before a long run, not just the night before.
- Eating something on runs over 90 minutes.
- Doing the [Stretching routine] after runs instead of skipping it.

[Priya] ran this race last year and said the hill at mile 9 is the hardest part. See [Running] for general notes.

# Half marathon training plan

Miles per day for the twelve weeks before the [Half marathon]. Mondays and Fridays are rest days, and Wednesdays are the [Stretching routine].

| Week | Tuesday | Thursday | Saturday | Sunday | Total |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | 3 easy | 3 easy | 5 long | 2 recovery | 13 |
| 2 | 3 easy | 4 tempo | 6 long | 2 recovery | 15 |
| 3 | 4 easy | 4 tempo | 7 long | 2 recovery | 17 |
| 4 | 3 easy | 3 easy | 5 long | 2 recovery | 13 |
| 5 | 4 easy | 5 intervals | 8 long | 3 recovery | 20 |
| 6 | 4 easy | 5 tempo | 9 long | 3 recovery | 21 |
| 7 | 5 easy | 5 intervals | 10 long | 3 recovery | 23 |
| 8 | 4 easy | 4 tempo | 7 long | 3 recovery | 18 |
| 9 | 5 easy | 6 tempo | 11 long | 3 recovery | 25 |
| 10 | 4 easy | 4 easy | 8 long | 2 recovery | 18 |
| 11 | 3 easy | 3 tempo | 5 long | 2 recovery | 13 |
| 12 | 3 easy | 2 easy | 13.1 race | rest | 18.1 |

See [Running] for general notes.

